8D
}}}
 (formal), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#a3-problem-solving"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
A3
}}}
 (one-page PADDER for sharing)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Recurring server crashes - Pinpoint timing, Analyze logs for patterns, Develop interim solutions (restart service) + permanent fix (increase memory), Monitor effectiveness} ### ICEBERG\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 I - Identify issue(s)  \line
C - Collect data and analyze situation  \line
E - Examine possible (root) causes  \line
B - Brainstorm solutions  \line
E - Execute solution(s)  \line
R - Review, evaluate, and adjust solutions  \line
G - Gather feedback  \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Complex, deep analysis (30\u8211-60 min); surface symptoms hide root causes; escalate from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#idea"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
IDEA
}}}
 when complexity grows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Pitfalls:} Too deep on simple (e.g.\u160 ?5\u8209 ?min password reset): start with IDEA, escalate if needed. Skipping G (feedback): prevents recurrence; complete the cycle.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56599 ? Combines well with:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#5-whys"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
5 Whys
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#ishikawa-fishbone-diagram"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Ishikawa
}}}
 (fishbone for Examine), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#8d-approach"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
8D
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#idea"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
IDEA
}}}
 (escalate if needed)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Network performance degradation - Identify slowness, Collect metrics (latency, packet loss), Examine causes (routing changes, bandwidth saturation), Brainstorm solutions, Execute, Review with team, Gather feedback from users} ### IDEA\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 I - Identify problem  \line
D - Develop Solution  \line
E - Execute Solution\line
A - Assess Solution  \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Quick, simple (2\u8211-5 min); crisis; use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#stop"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
STOP
}}}
 first if stressed.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Pitfalls:} Escalation: if past 10 min or multiple blockers \u8594 ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#iceberg"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ICEBERG
}}}
 or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#prepare"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PREPARE
}}}
. Skipping A: validate; prevents recurrence.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56599 ? Combines well with:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#stop"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
STOP
}}}
 (crisis), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#prepare"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PREPARE
}}}
/{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#iceberg"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ICEBERG
}}}
 (escalate)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i User can\u8217't access VPN - Identify (connection error), Develop (reset credentials), Execute (send new password), Assess (confirm access restored)} ### 5 Whys * Keep asking why until root causes are identified\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Root cause analysis; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#8d-approach"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
8D
}}}
 D4; combine with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#iceberg"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ICEBERG
}}}
 for deep dives.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Pitfalls:} Don\u8217't stop at symptoms (e.g.\u160 ?\u8220"DB slow\u8221")\u8212-drill to process/systemic failure. Multiple root causes: use 5 Whys per branch.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56599 ? Combines well with:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#iceberg"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ICEBERG
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#ishikawa-fishbone-diagram"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Ishikawa
}}}
 (branches, then \u8220"why\u8221" on each), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#8d-approach"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
8D
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Deployment failures - Why? Pipeline failed. Why? Tests timed out. Why? Database slow. Why? Index missing. Why? Schema change didn\u8217't include migration. Root cause: Missing migration validation step}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Ishikawa (Fishbone) Diagram\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Cause\u8211-effect; map multiple causes to one problem. Pairs with 5 Whys.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 1. State the problem (head of the fish)\line
2. Choose categories (e.g. 6 M's: Machine, Method, Material, Manpower, Measurement, Milieu/Environment)\line
3. Brainstorm causes in each category (bones)\line
4. Drill into "why" for significant causes (use 5 Whys on branches)\line
5. Identify root causes to address\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Multiple causes (5 Whys may miss branches); {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#8d-approach"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
8D
}}}
 D4 or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#iceberg"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ICEBERG
}}}
 Examine; brainstorm across people, process, tech, environment.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Pitfalls:} Too many bones: limit branches, focus on likely. Skipping drill-down: use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#5-whys"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
5 Whys
}}}
 on likely bones.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56599 ? Combines well with:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#5-whys"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
5 Whys
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#8d-approach"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
8D
}}}
 D4, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#iceberg"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ICEBERG
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#a3-problem-solving"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
A3
}}}
 (fishbone on A3)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Uptime drop - Problem (head): \u8220"Services unreachable.\u8221" Bones: Method (recent deploy), Machine (high CPU), Manpower (config change). Drill with 5 Whys on \u8220"recent deploy\u8221" \u8594 ? missing health-check in pipeline. Root cause: CI didn\u8217't run post-deploy checks.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 8D Approach\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Industry standard in automotive/manufacturing, adapted for IT incident management}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 D1 - Form a team  \line
D2 - Describe the problem  \line
D3 - Interim Containment Action (the "band-aid")  \line
D4 - Root Cause Analysis & Escape Point(s)  \line
D5 - Permanent Corrective Actions  \line
D6 - Implement & Validate Corrective Actions  \line
D7 - Prevent reoccurrence(s)  \line
D8 - Congratulate your team and close the loop (closure & celebration)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Critical incidents, formal resolution; documentation and prevention; team coordination (D1: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#raci"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
RACI
}}}
).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Pitfalls:} Stopping at D3: reach D7 or it recurs. Solo 8D: use D1 (Form a team) and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#raci"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
RACI
}}}
. Bureaucracy: use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#idea"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
IDEA
}}}
 or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#prepare"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PREPARE
}}}
 for non-critical.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56599 ? Combines well with:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#padder"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PADDER
}}}
 (D3), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#5-whys"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
5 Whys
}}}
+{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#ishikawa-fishbone-diagram"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Ishikawa
}}}
+{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#iceberg"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ICEBERG
}}}
 (D4), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#a3-problem-solving"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
A3
}}}
 (one-page 8D), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#raci"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
RACI
}}}
 (D1)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Data breach incident - Form security response team ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#raci"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
RACI
}}}
 roles), Describe scope, Contain (disable compromised accounts), Analyze root cause ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#5-whys"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
5 Whys
}}}
: phishing \u8594 ? no MFA \u8594 ? insufficient training), Implement MFA, Validate with penetration test, Prevent (mandatory security awareness), Celebrate team response}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 A3 Problem Solving\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Toyota\u8217's single-page (A3 size) structured problem-solving. Plan\u8211-Do\u8211-Check\u8211-Act on one sheet for clarity and alignment.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 1. Background & problem statement\line
2. Current state / gap\line
3. Goal / target state\line
4. Root cause analysis (use 5 Whys or Ishikawa)\line
5. Countermeasures\line
6. Implementation plan & follow-up (Check)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Share problem and plan on one page; lighter than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#8d-approach"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
8D
}}}
; recurring/medium severity; socialize {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#iceberg"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ICEBERG
}}}
 or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#padder"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PADDER
}}}
 output.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Pitfalls:} Cramming: if it doesn\u8217't fit, split or use 8D. Root cause box: use {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#5-whys"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
5 Whys
}}}
 or {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#ishikawa-fishbone-diagram"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Ishikawa
}}}
, not symptoms.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56599 ? Combines well with:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#5-whys"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
5 Whys
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#ishikawa-fishbone-diagram"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Ishikawa
}}}
 (root cause box), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#8d-approach"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
8D
}}}
 (A3 summarizes), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#iceberg"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ICEBERG
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#padder"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PADDER
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Sprint overruns - A3: Background (delivery slipping), Current state (scope creep, no Definition of Done), Goal (predictable sprints), Root cause (5 Whys \u8594 ? no intake prioritization), Countermeasures (backlog refinement + DoD), Plan (next 2 sprints). Share with product and eng leadership on one page.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 5Ps\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Poor planning produces pitiful products.} \u8212- Use as a reminder during planning; don\u8217't skip {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#prepare"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PREPARE
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55357 ?\u56522 ? Problem Analysis\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Frameworks for scope and impact.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 RACI\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Roles and responsibilities in problem-solving.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 R - Responsible (does the work)\line
A - Accountable (final approval)\line
C - Consulted (provides input)\line
I - Informed (kept updated)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Role confusion; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#8d-approach"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
8D
}}}
 D1 (Form a team); end of WAIT\u8594 ?BREATHE\u8594 ?PAUSE for conflict.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Pitfalls:} One \u8220"A\u8221" per task. Too many \u8220"C\u8221" slows decisions\u8212-only critical input.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Example:} {\i Infra upgrade: R=DevOps, A=Infra Manager, C=Security, I=All devs.} ### PESTEL {\i External factors that impact a problem or decision.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 P - Political\line
E - Economic\line
S - Sociocultural\line
T - Technological\line
E - Environmental\line
L - Legal\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Strategic planning, external factors; {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#scale-infrastructure-design"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
SCALE
}}}
 validation; architecture, compliance.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Cloud migration planning - Political (vendor lock-in concerns), Economic (cost optimization), Technological (API compatibility), Legal (data sovereignty requirements)}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 SWOT\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Internal and external factors for a problem or decision.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 S - Strengths\line
W - Weaknesses\line
O - Opportunities\line
T - Threats\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#prepare"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PREPARE
}}}
\u8217's \u8220"Evaluate options\u8221" step - {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#scale-infrastructure-design"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
SCALE
}}}
 design validation - Strategic decision making (1-2 hours)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Choosing deployment strategy - Strengths: automated rollback, Weaknesses: longer deployment time, Opportunities: canary testing, Threats: increased complexity} ### SET (Systems Engineering Triangle) {\i Good, Fast, Cheap: pick 2; the third suffers.} (Fast+Cheap\u8800 ?Good, Fast+Good\u8800 ?Cheap, Good+Cheap\u8800 ?Fast.)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Set expectations; end of SCALE\u8594 ?SWOT\u8594 ?PESTEL; architecture trade-offs.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Urgent security patch \u8212- Good+Fast \u8658 ? not cheap (overtime). Set expectations with leadership.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sebokwiki.org/wiki/Guide_to_the_Systems_Engineering_Body_of_Knowledge_(SEBoK)"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
SEBoK
}}}
}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Problem Resolution Threats\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Blockers before they derail.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 DICE\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 D - Delay\line
I - Incompetence\line
C - Conflict\line
E - External factors\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#idea"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
IDEA
}}}
\u8594 ?{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#dice"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
DICE
}}}
\u8594 ?{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#fate"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
FATE
}}}
 triage; blockers before execution; risk in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#prepare"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PREPARE
}}}
 phase.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 FATE\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 F - Funding\line
A - Allocation of resources \line
T - Time\line
E - Expertise\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Resource validation in triage; feasibility (10\u8211-30 min); after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#dice"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
DICE
}}}
 to validate resources.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 PEST\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 P - Political\line
E - Economic\line
S - Social\line
T - Technological\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} External threats to solutions; how to combat/remove.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55357 ?\u56803 ?\u65039 ? Communication & Conflict\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Calm, productive in difficult conversations.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 BREATHE\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 B - Breathe deeply and slowly   \line
R - Remain rational and listen  \line
E - Empathize with the other person's problem\line
A - Ask questions to understand  \line
T - Take a break if needed  \line
H - Hold back from reacting  \line
E - Express yourself calmly  \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} First when tensions rise (breathing regulates); WAIT\u8594 ?BREATHE\u8594 ?PAUSE\u8594 ?{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#raci"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
RACI
}}}
; if break needed \u8594 ? PAUSE.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Pitfalls:} Fake: breathing must be intentional and deep. Weaponizing: don\u8217't use dismissively; damages trust.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56599 ? Combines well with:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#wait"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
WAIT
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#pause"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PAUSE
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#stop"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
STOP
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Stakeholder disagrees with technical approach in meeting - Breathe deeply (regulate emotions), Remain rational, Empathize with their concerns, Ask clarifying questions, Take 5-minute break if tension escalates, Hold back defensive reactions, Express technical rationale calmly} ### PAUSE\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 P - Put things in perspective   \line
A - Acknowledge your feelings and theirs\line
U - Understand that you don't have to act/react right away  \line
S - Step Away from the situation  \line
E - Evaluate options and plan before acting   \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} - When BREATHE isn\u8217't enough - need physical separation - \u8220"Step Away\u8221" connects to WAIT philosophy - Combine with STOP for immediate stress de-escalation (5-20 min)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56599 ? Combines well with:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#breathe"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
BREATHE
}}}
 (first step), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#wait"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
WAIT
}}}
 (listen before speaking), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#stop"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
STOP
}}}
 (stress response)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Real-world example:} {\i Heated debate about architecture decision - Put in perspective (not life-or-death), Acknowledge both viewpoints have merit, Don\u8217't decide now, Step away for lunch break, Evaluate pros/cons offline, Return with structured comparison}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 WAIT\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i \u8220"Why am I troubled / talking?\u8221"} \u8212- Choose the right response; often listening is better.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} Before speaking; first in WAIT\u8594 ?BREATHE\u8594 ?PAUSE\u8594 ?RACI. Use BREATHE to regulate, then WAIT to choose.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Pitfalls:} Not \u8220"don\u8217't respond\u8221"\u8212-choose effectively. Don\u8217't use WAIT to avoid necessary communication or to dodge escalation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56599 ? Combines well with:} {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#breathe"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
BREATHE
}}}
, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#pause"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
PAUSE
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56523 ? Example:} {\i Accusatory email: Ask \u8220"Why troubled?\u8221" (ego?) and \u8220"Why talking?\u8221" (defend or resolve?). BREATHE+PAUSE; respond later with facts.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55358 ?\u56792 ? Stress & Resilience\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\i Calm and connected under pressure.}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 PACE\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 P - Physical activity\line
A - Avoiding unhealthy behaviors\line
C - Coping skills\line
E - Emotional awareness\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} First in PACE\u8594 ?ARIES\u8594 ?CALM\u8594 ?SHINE; immediate stress.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 STOP\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \f1 S - Step back\line
T - Take a deep breath\line
O - Observe what is happening\line
P - Pull back and put things in perspective\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u55357 ?\u56481 ? When to use:} - First response to ANY crisis - immediate stress management (2-5 min) - Start of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#stop"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
STOP
}}}
 \u8594 ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#trace-network-troubleshooting"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
TRACE
}}}
 \u8594 ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#debug-code--system-analysis"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
DEBUG
}}}
 \u8594 ? {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "#8d-approach"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
8D
}}}
 crisis response chain - Use with IDEA for quick problem resolution in crisis\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b \u9888 ?\u65039 ? Common pitfalls:} - {\b Going through motions} - Rushing through STOP without actually calming. The \u8220"Take a deep breath\u8221" must be intentional - pause for 3-5 seconds. - {\b Stopping at STOP} - Using STOP but not proceeding to next step (TRACE/IDEA). STOP is the foundation, not the solution.\par}
