{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Problem-Solving Methodologies\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b 8D (Eight Disciplines)} \u10003 ? \u8212- Ford Motor Company (1987). {\i Team Oriented Problem Solving Manual}. Evolved from TQM; in wide use in automotive and aerospace. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eight_disciplines_problem_solving"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Wikipedia
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b 5 Whys} \u9888 ? \u8212- Toyota Production System root cause technique; widely adapted across industries.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Ishikawa (Fishbone) Diagram} \u10003 ? \u8212- Ishikawa, K. (1960s). University of Tokyo. Cause\u8211-effect diagram; central to Japanese quality control and Toyota. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ishikawa_diagram"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Wikipedia
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b A3 Problem Solving} \u10003 ? \u8212- Toyota Production System. Single A3-page structured problem-solving (plan\u8211-do\u8211-check\u8211-act); one-page report for alignment. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A3_problem_solving"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Wikipedia
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b PADDER, ICEBERG, IDEA, PREPARE} \u8505 ? \u8212- Curated/educational problem-solving mnemonics for this collection.\sa180\par}
