{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b PESTEL} \u10003 ? \u8212- Aguilar, F. (1967). {\i Scanning the Business Environment}. Harvard; later extended to PESTLE/PESTEL (Legal, Environmental). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/background-development-pestel-analysis-biplab-paul-8hj0c"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Background
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b PEST} \u8505 ? \u8212- Four-factor variant (Political, Economic, Social, Technological); conceptually from the PESTEL lineage.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b SWOT} \u10003 ? \u8212- Humphrey, A. (1960s\u8211-70s). Stanford Research Institute (SRI International); developed with Fortune 500 planning research. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ninety.io/hubfs/Founders%20Framework%20-%20The%20SWOT%20Analysis%20and%20Strategic%20Planning%20Framework.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
